  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Multiprofile RNA is clearly stronger than single-profile RNA, and scvi_n200 multiprofile is the current best, but the transformer-vs-avgpool difference is small in both accuracy and F1. The cleanest missing comparison in the current RNA multiprofile grid is pca_n2000 with transformer aggregation, directly comparable to config_002. This experiment tests whether transformer aggregation generally improves multiprofile RNA or is specific to scvi_n200, without confounding from image modality or fusion. Under a limited budget, it is the most efficient next step because it isolates an important design choice, avoids overinterpreting a tiny performance gap, and solidifies the strongest unimodal direction before adding multimodal complexity."
